courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon successful completion of the course, students will be able to

1. understand and explain fundamental physics underlying semiconductor device technology;
2. perform analysis and design of common semiconductor devices based on fundamental principles;
3. describe how to analyze semiconductor devices and extract key device parameters by suitable experiments;
4. design and engineer materials and devices for special device and circuit applications;
5. decribe extended knowledge about semiconductor technology based on disordered semiconductors, such as flexible and printed electronics

Upon successful completion of this course, students will be able to:

1. have some basic ideas of artificial intelligence and machine learning;
2. know the medical applications of artificial intelligence and machine learning;
3. understand the limitations and possibilities of different approaches to artificial intelligence in medical image analysis;

Upon successful completion of this course, students will be able to:
1. Understand mainstream microelectronics & power electronics packaging format & process;
2. Understand the fundamentals of thermal management, mechanics & reliability;
3. Understand the principles of reliability tests & failure analysis techniques;
4. Use mainstream EDA tools in the industry to design and simulate the performance of electronics packages.

courses.feedback_evaluation:
We welcome students’ comments and feedback on the course. There are four main channels for collecting students’ feedback.

1. Mid-term course evaluation: An informal evaluation questionnaire conducted at the mid-term of this course covers the following areas:

1. Course organization and objectives;
2. Understanding fundamental contents;
3. Pace of teaching;
4. Method of lecture delivery;
5. Overall satisfaction.

2. Informal online contact: Students can send their comments via email to the course instructor, and the course instructor will follow up.

3. Individual consulting: Students are welcome to visit the course instructor during office hours. They can exchange opinions to make the course better suits the students’ needs.

4. Faculty course questionnaire: At the end of the course, students are required to provide feedback on different aspects related to teaching and learning of the course through a formal evaluation questionnaire.
